    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31638" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκᾰτόμ-πους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>, ὁ, ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hundred-footed</i>: in
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				718
			</span></i> (lyr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκατόμποδες
			Νηρηΐδες,</span> some take it literally to mean <i>the</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				50
			</span></i>
			<u>Nereids</u> (the number assigned to them by <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				264
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				6(5).6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				427
			</span></i>), others <i>the</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				100
			</span></i>
			<u>Nereids</u> (<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				116e
			</span></i>), others merely to express a notion of
		<i>multitude.</i></div>
